# Surface Slim Pen 2 (Bluetooth LE) top button, matched by input device name "Surface Slim Pen 2 Keyboard" (vendor/product unknown). Same chords as the Surface Pen (045E:0921):
# The pen does not report its button as a stylus button: it pairs as a tiny BLE keyboard and sends
# Win+F20 (click), Win+F19 (double-click) and Win+F18 (press and hold).
# This layout replaces Generic.kl for this device only: META (125) is intentionally NOT mapped, so the Windows-key
# chord does not reach Android, and the F-keys become stylus / system keys.
# STYLUS_BUTTON_TAIL is the Android 14+ key for "button at the tail end of a stylus"; SystemUI uses it to open the
# default note-taking app.

key 190   STYLUS_BUTTON_TAIL
key 189   SYSRQ
key 188   ASSIST
